  "workedSolution": "1. At $x = 1$: $y = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$. $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{3(x + 1) - (3x - 1)}{(x + 1)^{2}} = \\dfrac{4}{(x + 1)^{2}} = 1$. The normal has gradient $-1$: $y - 1 = -(x - 1)$, i.e. $y = 2 - x$, which meets $y = 0$ at $x = 2$.",
